  "narrative": "I assessed all twelve newly delivered comparisons against the 0.15 composite dependency-score-unit threshold, using the direction-signed estimates and 95% Welch intervals as reported. H111 is the most important new result: the signed feature_010-by-high-feature_018 interaction estimate is 0.766 with interval 0.550 to 0.981, so the feature_010 positive contrast is meaningfully smaller in high feature_018 than in its complement. This accepts as a central effect-modification claim and justifies independent validation because multiple related subgroup comparisons have already been examined and this interaction is now a major branch in the feature_010 story. H94 also strongly accepts: feature_010 positivity has a signed positive contrast of 0.828 with interval 0.714 to 0.941 among feature_018<=-0.5, consistent with the low-feature_018 tail driving part of the non-high-feature_018 positive association. H115 accepts the feature_010 positive association in mid feature_036 (0.405; 0.258 to 0.552), broadening the feature_010 map beyond high and low feature_038/feature_018 extremes. H112 accepts a positive feature_010 contrast among feature_003-positive and non-high feature_038 individuals (0.598; 0.361 to 0.835), but the exposed cell has only 57 observations and the claim involves two conditioning variables, so I accept it at discovery level but defer it rather than treat it as settled. H113 and H114 accept feature_003 lowering within high feature_036 combined with high feature_018 (0.791; 0.535 to 1.047) and high feature_038 (0.562; 0.285 to 0.838), respectively. These are scientifically useful because they show the high-feature_036 feature_003 signal can persist inside high-signature strata, but both exposed cells are small (39 and 44) and these are post-hoc joint subgroup claims after many tests, so I accept them only as discovery evidence and defer further weight. H97 is not supportive of a meaningful feature_003 lowering effect in the broad feature_018<=0.49 context: the signed estimate is 0.106, below threshold, with interval 0.015 to 0.198. Because the interval crosses the meaningful-effect threshold, I leave it unresolved and deferred rather than reject it outright. The feature_037 breadth claims are all strong: mid feature_036 H99 estimate 0.811 (0.704 to 0.919), mid feature_018 H102 estimate 0.837 (0.731 to 0.943), mid feature_038 H103 estimate 0.815 (0.711 to 0.920), non-high feature_038 H107 estimate 0.802 (0.723 to 0.881), and non-high feature_036 H108 estimate 0.810 (0.731 to 0.890). All intervals are well above the 0.15-unit threshold and support the conclusion that feature_037 positivity is strongly associated with lower outcome_001 across much of the measured feature space. Overall, these remain unadjusted associations in the supplied dataset, with overlapping subgroup searches and residual multiplicity risk; they are not causal effects or generalizable claims.",
  "research_notes": "Updated dataset-specific map. feature_037 positivity is broadly and strongly associated with lower outcome_001: accepted marginal validated R38/R39, accepted high/low feature_018 R61/R62, accepted mid feature_036 R75, mid feature_018 R76, mid feature_038 R77, non-high feature_038 R78, and non-high feature_036 R79. feature_003 positivity lowering is concentrated in high feature_036 contexts: accepted/validated high feature_036 R21/R26, accepted feature_037-negative high feature_036 R45/R52, accepted triple feature_037-negative/feature_010-negative/high feature_036 R58/R66, accepted joint high feature_036 + high feature_018 R70 and high feature_036 + high feature_038 R71; non-high feature_036 complements remain rejected R59/R60. Broad feature_018<=0.49 feature_003 effect is only below-threshold/unresolved R74. feature_010 positivity raises outcome_001 overall and in many strata; new evidence accepts low feature_018 R73 and mid feature_036 R72, and strongly supports a high-feature_018 attenuation interaction R68. Existing evidence also supports non-high feature_038 R55, low feature_038 R56, mid feature_038 R57, and feature_018<=0.49 R64, while high feature_038 simple effect is near-null but imprecise R54 and high feature_018 positive simple effect is rejected R63. Current validation request: H111, because this new feature_018-by-feature_010 interaction is central and discovery-only. Next useful analyses: H70/H89/H63/H64 to complete feature_037 breadth across high/low feature_038 and feature_036; H116/H117 to test feature_003 high-feature_036 signal in non-high feature_018 and non-high feature_038; H118 to test feature_010 in high feature_018 but non-high feature_038; H104/H105/H106 for remaining mid/complement strata; H21/H22 for feature_003 interactions with feature_038 and feature_018. Do not request validation for already validated exact claims. All conclusions remain unadjusted associations in the supplied dataset, noncausal, and not generalizable.",
